# File sync after edits

## VBA (`.bas` / `.frm` / `.cls`)

After editing any existing VBA module/form on disk, push it live with:

```
python mcp-server/hot_reload.py <path(s)>
```

Do **not** ask the engineer to delete+re-import for routine code updates. Hot-reload replaces `CodeModule` text in the open MicroStation VBA project in place.

### NEVER hot-reload while VBA is busy

Documented live (`dev-notes/agent-log.md`, 2026-08-02 Tier1-3): VBA IDE state `[running]` or `[break]` **blocks** hot-reload; forcing COM CodeModule edits while a bridge op / GetInput / hung procedure is executing can **wedge the project or crash MicroStation**.

### VBA errors / break / stuck macros — agent always resets (never ask)

Standing engineer preference: **you** clear VBA problems. Do not ask the engineer to
Reset, Ctrl+Break, or dismiss VBA OK dialogs.

Use `mcp-server/ord_uia.py`: `ensure_vba_idle` / `reset_vba` / `dismiss_vba_ok`
(CommandBars Run→Reset on the active project, including `Test.mvba`). Also
`CadInputQueue.SendReset` + Escape when ORD is armed (`File Saving > …`, etc.).
Maintenance clears may set `QA_ALLOW_NO_TASK=1`. Status-bar
`VBA interface error: unable to run macro - 0x800adf09` is the same class of
problem — reset/clear it yourself before continuing bridge or UI work.

Before every `hot_reload.py` call:
1. If a bridge/agent tool call, keyin batch, or VBA procedure may still be running — **stop** and **Reset VBA yourself** (`ensure_vba_idle` / `reset_vba`) first.
2. Do **not** retry hot-reload in a loop against COM errors while MicroStation/VBA looks stuck — that makes crashes more likely.
3. After a failed hot-reload that leaves every subsequent reload COM-failing: Reset yourself, then re-import the affected modules from disk (File Sync Protocol) if still blocked.

Still needs a **manual Import** (not hot-reload) when:
- the component does not exist in the IDE yet (brand-new file)
- adding/changing **UserForm Designer controls** (layout is not CodeModule)

If MicroStation is closed or hot-reload fails after a clean Reset, say so and fall back to the File Sync Protocol in `CLAUDE.md`.

## Python (`mcp-server/chat_driver.py`, `wztc_ops.py`, `view_capture.py`, etc.)

Hot-reload does **not** apply. After editing any `mcp-server/*.py` (or other Python the live agent imports), **you** restart the driver — do **not** ask the engineer to do it:

```
python mcp-server/restart_chat_driver.py
```

That script refuses if a turn looks in-flight (last `chat-log.tsv` line not FINAL/ERROR); use `--force` only when you've confirmed it's safe. Do not claim a VBA hot-reload picked up Python changes.
